      "solution": "a, b, c, d = map(int, input().split())\nn, m = map(int, input().split())\n\nvisite = [0] * 100001\nfile = [n]\nvisite[n] = 1\ni = 0\n\nwhile i < len(file):\n    v = file[i]\n    i += 1\n    if v == m:\n        print(\"1\")\n        exit()\n    for nv in (v + a, v - b, v * c, v // d if d != 0 and v % d == 0 else -1):\n        if 0 <= nv <= 100000 and not visite[nv]:\n            visite[nv] = 1\n            file.append(nv)\n\nprint(\"0\")",
      "statement": "You are given a starting number [[N]] and a target number [[M]].\nThe goal is to apply a sequence of operations starting from [[N]] in order to obtain the value [[M]].\n\nThere are <<4 possible operations>>:\n    • add [[A]],\n    • subtract [[B]],\n    • multiply by [[C]],\n    • divide by [[D]], provided that the result is an integer,\n\nwhere [[A]], [[B]], [[C]], and [[D]] are integers given in the input.\nYou need to note that all intermediate results must remain within the interval {{[0, 100000]}}.\n\nDetermine whether there exists a sequence of operations that allows you to go from the starting number to the target number.\n\nNote: The operations can repeat.",
